<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Ishaq Inju</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1357</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Ishaq Inju was the last Injuid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a>, governing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> from about 1343. A cultivated and lavish ruler, he was visited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta">Ibn Battuta</a> and patronised the poets <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafez">Hafez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ubayd-zakani">Ubayd Zakani</a>. The Muzaffarid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mubariz-al-din-muhammad">Mubariz al-Din Muhammad</a> took Shiraz in 1353 and had him executed in 1357.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-ishaq-inju.jpg" alt="Abu Ishaq Inju" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shiraz, 1352-53 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frontispiece_(rulers_enthroned)._Firdaws%C4%AB,_Stephens_Sh%C4%81hn%C4%81ma._Probably_Shiraz,_1352%E2%80%9353.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
